      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "`DesignatedRequirement` (string) *(required)*: The code signature designated requirement of the app using the per-app VPN.",
      "contextAfter": "`MatchTools` ([AppToAppLayerVPNMapping.AppLayerVPNMappingItem.MatchToolsItem]): An array of dictionaries. Each dictionary specifies a per-app VPN rule. Use this property to restrict this per-app VPN rule to only match the app’s spawned *helper tool* network traffic. For example, to match network traffic that the `curl` command generates when run from the Terminal.app, create an app mapping payload for Terminal.app and set the payload’s `MatchTools` key to an array that contains a dictionary that matches the `curl` command-line tool. If you don’t specify the `MatchTools` key, this per-app VPN rule matches all network traffic that the matching app and its spawned helper tools generate.",
